Z||000002||GTDude||12-18-2001||10:33 PM||||I'm positive I've seen ads for it....but it's been quite a while.  Might check out putting 1.6 rockers on it instead.  Does virgually the same thing.  Prob have to get a set of 16 tho for the 301 pont engine.  You can prob split a set with someone else with out much problem.<P><BR>Phil Pettus<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Blacktree||12-19-2001||12:44 AM||||Keep in mind that the stock rocker arm ratio for the Duke is 1.75:1. Dropping in some 1.6 ratio rockers will improve low-range torque, but will cause the engine to lose power in the medium-to-high RPM range.<P>So far, the only aftermarket cams I've found for the Duke are the PAW (performance automotive warehouse) house brand, and they're made for the 1979-1984 Dukes (carbureted).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||12-19-2001||01:23 AM||||Call up DeltaCam, I bet they'll make you anything you want.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.deltacam.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.deltacam.com/</A> <P>------------------<BR>Its never going to be finished...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig2_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
